meta {
  name: 9c3. Verify X-Userinfo spoofing is rejected on the portal-backend route (→ 401)
  type: http
  seq: 25
  tags: [
    requires-nifi
  ]
}

get {
  url: {{apisixApiUrl}}/v1/datasets/{{sagaDataSetId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Userinfo: eyJzdWIiOiJmb3JnZWQtYWRtaW4tMTIzNDUifQ
}

tests {
  test("A forged X-Userinfo cannot impersonate a user on the portal-backend route (401, not 200/403)", function() {
    // Counterpart to 9c2 (saga-created dataset payload route) on the portal-backend MANAGEMENT route
    // (the gateway's /v1/* catch-all → portal-backend). Both routes reference the same plugin_config
    // (serverless-pre-function strips client X-Userinfo before OPA). The forged header claims
    // sub="forged-admin-12345" against the metadata endpoint /v1/datasets/{id}.
    //
    // Metadata is not open data, so an anonymous caller is denied. The discriminator: if the strip
    // works, OPA sees no userinfo → 401. If the forged header reached OPA, it would be treated as an
    // (authenticated-but-unknown) identity → 403 (or, worse, a real grant if the sub matched). Exactly
    // 401 proves the strip is active on the portal-backend route too, not only the dataset route.
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(401);
  });
}

docs {
  **Saga step 9c3** — X-Userinfo spoofing guard on the **portal-backend** route.

  The Issue requires the identity-header strip to hold on portal-backend **and** saga-created dataset
  routes. 9c2 covers the dataset payload route; this step covers the portal-backend management route
  (`/v1/datasets/{id}`, reached via the gateway's `/v1/*` catch-all). It sends an unauthenticated
  request with a **forged** `X-Userinfo` and asserts **401** — the `serverless-pre-function` cleared
  the header before OPA, so the forged identity never took effect.

  **Precondition:** runs while the dataset is protected (before 9f).
}
